  CorporateLanguageTerm(
    term: 'Revenue',
    fullForm: '—',
    meaning: 'Money earned from selling products or services before deducting costs.',
    whereSeen: 'P&L, sales reviews',
    bridge: 'Revenue is not the same as profit or cash collected.',
    category: 'Finance & Accounting',
    priorityTier: 1,
    indianContext: 'Every P&L review in an Indian company starts with the revenue line, and sales, finance and leadership all track it closely because it signals whether the business is winning in the market, even before costs are considered. Managers often get asked to explain revenue movements by region, product line or client before anyone discusses profitability, so being fluent in how revenue is recognised and reported matters early in a career transition.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'Think of revenue like the total tonnage or stores moved through a supply chain in a given period — it tells you activity and throughput, but says nothing yet about whether the operation was efficient or sustainable. A high-activity month looks impressive on paper the same way high revenue does, until you ask what it cost to generate.',
