    bridge: 'Shows economics before many overheads.',
    category: 'Finance & Accounting',
    indianContext: 'Gross profit is a first checkpoint finance teams use in margin analysis to see whether the core selling proposition is economically sound before overheads like rent, salaries and marketing are even considered. Product and category managers in Indian retail, manufacturing and services firms watch this number closely when deciding pricing or which product lines to expand.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'It resembles calculating the net gain of an operation after direct expenditure on ammunition, fuel and rations for that specific mission, before counting the standing cost of maintaining the base or garrison that supported it. It isolates whether the mission itself was worth running, separate from the overhead of running the unit.',
    dialogueSnippet: '"Gross profit on this product line is healthy, so the pricing problem must be sitting somewhere in overheads."',
    trapForOfficers: 'A newcomer might assume gross profit is the company\'s actual take-home profit and stop analysis there, not realising that rent, salaries, admin and financing costs still have to be subtracted before you know if the business as a whole is profitable.',
  ),
  CorporateLanguageTerm(
    term: 'Gross Margin',
