    category: 'Finance & Accounting',
    priorityTier: 2,
    indianContext: 'Because gross margin is a percentage, Indian pricing and finance teams use it to compare very different products, business units or time periods on a like-for-like basis rather than comparing raw rupee amounts, which can be misleading given differing scale. It routinely comes up when leadership asks why one product category is more attractive to invest in than another.',
