    bridge: 'Often used alongside NPV rather than instead of it.',
    category: 'Finance & Accounting',
    priorityTier: 3,
    indianContext: 'IRR is quoted alongside NPV in Indian investment committee discussions as a percentage return figure that\'s often easier for non-finance stakeholders to grasp intuitively than an absolute NPV number, though experienced finance professionals caution against relying on it alone. It frequently comes up when comparing competing capital projects against each other or against a company\'s cost of capital.',
