    category: 'Finance & Accounting',
    priorityTier: 2,
    indianContext: 'ROE is a key metric Indian investors and finance teams use to judge how efficiently a company is using shareholders\' money to generate profit, and it\'s frequently compared across companies in the same sector to judge relative management effectiveness. It shows up regularly in investor presentations and annual report commentary.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'This is similar to measuring how effectively a unit converts its allotted core resources into mission outcomes, rather than just looking at total output — a smaller, leaner unit that achieves proportionally more with what it was given can outperform a larger one on this measure.',
    dialogueSnippet: '"Our ROE has improved this year, mainly because profit grew faster than the equity base did."',
