    dialogueSnippet: '"We\'ve taken on more leverage to fund the expansion, so the board wants tighter monitoring of our debt covenants."',
    trapForOfficers: 'Officers might hear "leverage" used only in its everyday sense of gaining an advantage, and miss that in finance it specifically refers to debt-funded risk, where more leverage means both higher potential upside and higher potential downside.',
