    indianContext: 'JIT is a manufacturing philosophy where materials arrive just before they\'re needed rather than being stockpiled in advance, which frees up working capital and warehouse space but makes production highly dependent on supplier reliability — a lesson many Indian manufacturers relearned painfully during recent supply disruptions. Companies weigh JIT\'s cost benefits against the resilience benefits of holding some buffer stock, and that balance shifts depending on how volatile the supply environment is.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'This is close to minimising forward stockpiles and instead timing resupply precisely to need — efficient in stable conditions, but it leaves very little margin for error if the supply line is disrupted, which is exactly the trade-off any logistics planner weighs between efficiency and resilience.',
