    whereSeen: 'Projects, contracts',
    bridge: 'A tangible or clearly defined outcome.',
    category: 'Project & Program Management',
    priorityTier: 1,
    indianContext: 'Contracts and project plans define specific deliverables tied to payment milestones and client reviews, and performance is judged against whether those defined outputs were produced, not just against effort spent. Status reports typically list deliverables by name and due date.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'It is comparable to a specified output of a task — the finished report, structure or capability that must actually be produced and handed over, distinct from the effort or activity that went into producing it.',
    dialogueSnippet: '"Send me the deliverable list for this sprint so I can update the client status report."',
    trapForOfficers: 'Officers might describe effort or activity ("we worked hard on the integration") as if it were a deliverable, when corporates expect a discrete, verifiable output or artifact that someone can point to and check off.',
  ),
  CorporateLanguageTerm(
    term: 'Milestone',
    fullForm: '—',
