    bridge: 'Business acceptance before go-live.',
    category: 'Project & Program Management',
    priorityTier: 2,
    indianContext: 'Before a system goes live, business users test it in a dedicated UAT environment to confirm it actually meets their practical, day-to-day needs, separate from and after the technical testing done by developers. Go-live is typically blocked until business stakeholders formally sign off on UAT.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'It is comparable to a trial of new equipment or a new procedure by the actual operating troops before full induction, rather than relying only on a technical bench test carried out by the manufacturer.',
    dialogueSnippet: '"We can\'t go live until the business team has signed off on UAT, technical testing alone isn\'t enough."',
    trapForOfficers: 'Officers might conflate UAT with the developer or QA testing that happens earlier, when UAT is specifically business-user validation, and skipping it even after technical tests pass is a common and costly failure mode.',
  ),
  CorporateLanguageTerm(
