    meaning: 'Small-scale demonstration to test whether an idea or technology is feasible.',
    whereSeen: 'Technology, innovation',
    bridge: 'Tests feasibility rather than proving a full business case.',
    category: 'Project & Program Management',
    priorityTier: 2,
    indianContext: 'Technology and innovation teams run a POC to check whether an idea or technology is feasible in principle before committing real budget, deliberately keeping it small-scale, quick and low-risk rather than production-ready. Vendors are often asked to run a POC before a full contract is signed.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'It is comparable to a limited trial of a new tactic or piece of equipment in a controlled setting, aimed at establishing that it works in principle before any wider adoption is considered.',
    dialogueSnippet: '"Let\'s run a two-week POC with one vendor before we commit real budget to this."',
    trapForOfficers: 'Officers might expect a POC to be built to full production or security standards, when a POC is deliberately minimal by design, and judging it — or reusing it as-is — as if it were the final solution misreads its purpose.',
  ),
  CorporateLanguageTerm(
    term: 'MVP',
    fullForm: 'Minimum Viable Product',
    meaning: 'Simplest product version that can be released to learn from real users while providing enough value to test the concept.',
