    category: 'Project & Program Management',
    priorityTier: 2,
    indianContext: 'Technology, product and project teams use agile ways of working to plan and adapt in short cycles rather than committing to one rigid multi-month plan, revisiting priorities frequently as requirements or feedback change. It shapes how work is planned, reviewed and re-prioritised across the team\'s calendar.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'It is comparable to a flexible, decentralised planning approach that adapts frequently to ground truth rather than executing one fixed order from start to finish without revision.',
    dialogueSnippet: '"We\'re working agile now, so priorities can genuinely shift every two weeks based on what we\'re learning."',
    trapForOfficers: 'Officers might read "agile" as a synonym for unplanned or undisciplined, when it is actually a structured method with its own roles, ceremonies and discipline — shorter cycles, not less rigor.',
  ),
  CorporateLanguageTerm(
    term: 'Scrum',
    fullForm: '—',
    meaning: 'A specific Agile framework using defined roles, events and iterative work cycles.',
