    meaning: 'Prioritised list of work, features, fixes or requirements awaiting execution.',
    whereSeen: 'Product, Agile',
    bridge: 'Dynamic work queue.',
    category: 'Project & Program Management',
    indianContext: 'Product and agile teams maintain the backlog as a living, prioritised list of work, with a product owner deciding what moves up based on changing business needs, reprioritised continuously rather than fixed in advance. A growing backlog is a normal, expected state rather than a sign of trouble.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'It is comparable to a running list of pending tasks or requirements waiting to be actioned as resources and priority allow, similar to a maintenance or training backlog that gets worked down over time.',
    dialogueSnippet: '"That request is going into the backlog, we\'ll prioritise it properly in the next planning session."',
