    bridge: 'Can include technical, behavioural and leadership capabilities.',
    category: 'HR & People',
    indianContext: 'Competency frameworks define the specific behaviours and capabilities expected at each role level — things like stakeholder management, strategic thinking or technical depth — and are used across recruitment interviews, performance appraisals and promotion panels to assess candidates against a consistent standard rather than gut feel. HR and L&D jointly maintain these frameworks and update them as business needs evolve.',
    militaryEquivalent: 'Competency frameworks are similar in spirit to the qualities and skills assessed in confidential reports and promotion boards — leadership, judgement, technical proficiency — except corporate competency frameworks are usually written down explicitly with defined behavioural indicators an interviewer or appraiser scores against, rather than largely relying on a reporting officer\'s overall subjective assessment.',
    dialogueSnippet: '"The interview panel is scoring candidates against five core competencies — make sure your answers give specific examples for each one."',
    trapForOfficers: 'Officers used to being assessed holistically through confidential reports may under-prepare for competency-based interviews, not realizing they\'re expected to structure specific, evidence-based examples ("tell me about a time when...") mapped explicitly to each named competency.',
